---
title: "Company setup: onboarding"
description: Take over a new client with the onboarding wizard — learn prior years, complete the items before opening and the items before closing.
sidebar:
  order: 4
  label: "Setup: onboarding"
---

When a new client is taken over, several company-level settings must first be given by a person. They are collected under **Company setup › Onboarding**. The top line shows the progress, for example "Onboarding: before opening 2/3 · before closing 0/3". Select **Continue setup** to open the **Onboarding wizard**.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/setup-onboarding-wizard" caption="The onboarding wizard: step 4 of 7, Bank accounts." /%}

## The seven steps

The wizard shows one step per screen. The steps are listed on the left in two groups, **Before opening** and **Before closing**. The steps can be done in any order; the wizard opens at the first step that is not completed. Use **Previous** and **Next** to move between steps.

{% steps %}

1. **Learn prior years.** Upload the general ledgers and financial statements of earlier years and select **Learn prior years**. Operon learns the account mapping, the bank accounts, the GST registration and the opening balances from them. What it learns is only a suggestion: a suggestion takes effect only once a person confirms it. To learn again after more files are added, select **Learn again**. A company without a prior-year general ledger (newly incorporated, or kept for the first time) declares **No prior-year general ledger (newly incorporated or first-time bookkeeping)**. This step blocks neither opening nor closing.

2. **GST registration** (before opening): whether the company is GST-registered and from which date. This determines whether tax is split out.

3. **Opening balances** (before opening): where the books start. Confirm the balance sheet at the takeover date line by line, and the aged lists of receivables and payables.

4. **Bank accounts** (before opening): the register of the company's bank and wallet accounts, and the opening balance of each account. The register determines which account a statement belongs to. On the **Bank opening balances** tab, confirm each account's opening balance from its statement, for example with **Post opening balance …** (the button shows the amount).

5. **Payroll register** (before closing): the employees of the company, or the declaration **No salaries paid this financial year**.

6. **Period-end rules** (before closing): a decision for each category of period-end rule, such as depreciation or foreign-currency revaluation: a confirmed policy, or the declaration **The company has no such category**.

7. **Fixed assets** (before closing): the fixed asset register, or the declaration **The company has no fixed assets**.

{% /steps %}

Uploads are available at any time, but reading and posting wait until the three items before opening (GST registration, opening balances and bank accounts) are complete. When they are complete, select **Go to upload** to go to step 1 Documents.

{% aside type="caution" %}
Until the three items before opening are complete, the documents of the period cannot be read or posted. Until the items before closing are complete, the period cannot be closed, not even by a manager's override.
{% /aside %}

## Example

ABC PTE. LTD. is taken over from 1 July 2026. The accountant confirms GST registration from 1 January 2024, enters the balance sheet at 30 June 2026 and the aged lists of receivables and payables, and registers one bank account, UOB SGD current. On **Bank opening balances**, Operon suggests an opening balance of SGD 52,480.00, the balance printed on the first statement; the accountant checks it and selects **Post opening balance 52,480.00**. The documents of the third quarter can then be read.
